  "notes": "Bad Boy male group from *Making the Band*, on Hitmen-era productions and later Bryan-Michael Cox, 2008–2010. The research gives \"71–109; ballads 71–76 half-time, one uptempo at 109\", and the ballad band is the base with `halfTime` true; the single 109 outlier is a different backbeat class. Three drum deltas from \"808/clap bed with the clap on beat 3 at the ballad tempo, offbeat 808 hats, snare-roll pickup\": a kick with `lockTo808` at 0.55 and a real tresillo lean, a clap stacked on beat 3, and an offbeat shaker/snap bed at three to five hits a bar against a hat lane at 0.12 — plus a 16th `snareRoll` ladder for the pickup. This is a true 808 model — \"808 sub on the root with a slide, long decay\" — so `drums.bass808` takes role `bassline` and there is no `bassline` block. Harmony splits the way the entry says the board does: \"piano/Rhodes-led 4-chord cycles in the Cox school, two-chord vamps on the Hitmen cuts\", so both a four-chord and a two-chord family are authored, with `maxChords` 4 and a 0.16 triad share. \"Five-part male harmony with a gospel-derived spread and a belted lead, moderate note-density\" is a twenty-nine-semitone melody register with an arch-leaning contour and a counter at −12 sharing weight between `octave_echo` and `sustain_pad`. ⚠ Confidence is **low**: the research rates the entry medium-low and marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ Every velocity, density and ramp number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"minor-mode with maj7 colour [LOW-CONF]\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
